# Loan Review
**Borrowing review | affordability and repayment milestones**

The first-year and lifetime totals reconcile the payment schedule to the contractual loan calculation. The ten-year balance is useful when considering a future move; it does not include sale costs or changes in property value.

| Metric || Value |
| --- || --- |
| First-year schedule interest || = sum(@[Amortization::E2:E13]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| First-year cumulative interest || = -cumipmt(@["Loan"::["Monthly rate","Value"]], @["Loan"::["Payment periods","Value"]], @["Loan"::["Principal","Value"]], 1, 12) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Interest difference || = B2 - B3 {:.8f} |
| First-year schedule principal || = sum(@[Amortization::F2:F13]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| First-year cumulative principal || = -cumprinc(@["Loan"::["Monthly rate","Value"]], @["Loan"::["Payment periods","Value"]], @["Loan"::["Principal","Value"]], 1, 12) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Principal difference || = B5 - B6 {:.8f} |
| First payment principal || = -ppmt(@["Loan"::["Monthly rate","Value"]], 1, @["Loan"::["Payment periods","Value"]], @["Loan"::["Principal","Value"]]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Effective annual rate || = effect(@["Loan"::["Annual nominal rate","Value"]], 12) {:.2%} |
| Lifetime schedule interest || = sum(@[Amortization::E2:E361]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Lifetime cumulative interest || = -cumipmt(@["Loan"::["Monthly rate","Value"]], @["Loan"::["Payment periods","Value"]], @["Loan"::["Principal","Value"]], 1, 360) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Lifetime interest difference || = B10 - B11 {:.8f} |
| Total principal repaid || = sum(@[Amortization::F2:F361]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Final balance || = @[Amortization::G361] {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Balance after ten years || = @[Amortization::G121] {:,.2f} {::>} |
| First-year interest share || = B2 / @["Annual Ownership"::["2027","Loan payments"]] {:.1%} |
| Monthly ownership budget || = @["Loan"::["Monthly ownership budget","Value"]] {:,.2f} {::>} |

# Rate Comparison
**Payment sensitivity | 15-year and 30-year borrowing**

The same purchase deposit is used at each rate. Shorter terms reduce lifetime interest but increase the monthly commitment. Closing costs and annual ownership costs are not included in this comparison.

